- .ifdef inside struct/union

Known defects and follow-ups:

- Deferred nonpositive storage counts outside explicit user-type initializer
  padding can produce oversized zero fills in object output. Cover omitted
  user-type fields and initialized/omitted built-in arrays; distinguish invalid
  counts from valid zero padding before object encoding.
- Forward alias chains in ordinary operands can fail in pure-binary output or
  produce objects with invalid local symbol indices. sizeof(label) also cannot
  resolve multi-level forward aliases in storage counts.
- Union fields reject named counts even when the constant is already defined,
  then can report a cascaded error at the initializer.
- The user-type array count resolver expands repeated aliases as trees. Cache
  resolved symbols per evaluation to avoid exponential work while preserving
  assignment-time values and cycle detection.
- Repeated aggregate instances still require quadratic statement-list work,
  including when counts are literal. Profile list replacement and merging.
